.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-GET-OBJECT-COUNT 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-get-object-count \- return the number of objects in a bucket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm get-object-count
.BR \-\-bucket | \-b
.I ERN
.SH DESCRIPTION
Returns the bucket's stored object count. That figure is a running
total, moved as objects are written and removed rather than counted on
demand, so this costs one document read whatever the bucket holds.
.PP
It is always the whole bucket, and it is only as current as the last
time the monitoring module recomputed it from what the bucket actually
holds \- every
.I euclid.modules.emo.bucket\-count\-period
seconds.
.BR euclid-cli-esm-count-objects (1)
counts for real, and is the one that takes a prefix.
.PP
This command accepted a
.B \-\-prefix
until euclid 1.0.73 and silently ignored it, answering the whole
bucket's figure regardless. The option is gone rather than honoured,
because the stored total is a property of the bucket and there is no
per-prefix one to read.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bucket " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the bucket. Required.
.PP
The bucket may be given by
.B name
instead of by ERN, in which case it is resolved in your session's account
and namespace; see
.B NAMES AND ERNS
in
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A summary
.RI ( "{ern, count}" )
is printed as JSON, where
.I count
is the number of matching objects.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or no
bucket with that ERN exists.
.SH EXAMPLES
Count every object in a bucket:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm get-object-count \e
    --bucket ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000:bucket:reports
.fi
.RE
.PP
Count only objects under a given key prefix \- which is the other
command:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm count-objects \e
    --bucket ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000:bucket:reports \e
    --prefix 2025/
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm-count-objects (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-list-objects (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-get-bucket-size (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-purge-bucket (1)
